# A qualified name needs no `use` (Jimmy's ruling QN, "follow Rust", which overrules
# Semantics ch. 6's "only through `use`"): `Words.Name`, a function, `Words.Unit`, a type
# and its constructor `Words.Metres`, and `Ui.Label`, a tag, are each reached by the
# module's name with no `use` line; `use Shapes.*` brings `Double` in bare. The other
# direction is neg/bare-name-no-use. Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject
# to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Words
mod Shapes
use Shapes.*

Long: fn Words.Unit -> Bool
fn Long (Words.Metres) = True
fn Long (Words.Feet) = False

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Words.Name (Double 2)} {Long Words.Metres}")
